---
title: Sidebar
description: The side nav — grouped links with icons, collapsible trees, counts. It collapses to an icon rail and, on a phone, its links move into the menu panel. The one on the left of this page is it.
eyebrow: Navigation
source: src/layout/sidenav.css
---
<h2>Groups and links</h2>
<p>One class, <code>im-navlink</code>, inside <code>im-navgroup</code>s. The current page is <code>aria-current="page"</code> — no "active" class to keep in step.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 17rem"}}
<nav aria-label="Example">
	<div class="im-navgroup">
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#groups-and-links" aria-current="page">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#groups-and-links">{{> "icons/book-open"}}<span>Journal</span><small>48</small></a>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#groups-and-links">{{> "icons/video"}}<span>Videos</span><span class="im-badge im-badge-accent">New</span></a>
	</div>
</nav>
{{/example}}

<h2>Titled groups</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 17rem"}}
<nav class="im-stack im-stack-sm" aria-label="Example">
	<div class="im-navgroup">
		<p class="im-navgroup-title">Writing</p>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#titled-groups">{{> "icons/book-open"}}<span>Journal</span></a>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#titled-groups">{{> "icons/tag"}}<span>Topics</span></a>
	</div>
	<div class="im-navgroup">
		<p class="im-navgroup-title">About</p>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#titled-groups">{{> "icons/user"}}<span>Me</span></a>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="#titled-groups">{{> "icons/mail"}}<span>Contact</span></a>
	</div>
</nav>
{{/example}}

<h2>Tree</h2>
<p>A collapsible group is a native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>: keyboard support, open state and find-in-page all come from the browser, with no script. Add <code>open</code> to start expanded — do that for the branch containing the current page.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 17rem"}}
<nav class="im-navgroup" aria-label="Example">
	<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a>
	<details class="im-navtree" open>
		<summary class="im-navlink">{{> "icons/layers"}}<span>Projects</span></summary>
		<div class="im-navtree-items">
			<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree" aria-current="page"><span>Case studies</span></a>
			<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree"><span>Work log</span></a>
			<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree"><span>Open source</span><small>12</small></a>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details class="im-navtree">
		<summary class="im-navlink">{{> "icons/map-pin"}}<span>Travel</span></summary>
		<div class="im-navtree-items">
			<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree"><span>Trips</span></a>
			<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree"><span>Wishlist</span></a>
		</div>
	</details>
	<a class="im-navlink" href="#tree">{{> "icons/mail"}}<span>Contact</span></a>
</nav>
{{/example}}

<h2>Three states</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit im-grid-sm">
	<div class="im-stack im-stack-xs"><div class="mini-shell"><span>bar</span><span>nav</span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted"><strong>Open</strong> — from <code>lg</code>, by default</p></div>
	<div class="im-stack im-stack-xs"><div class="mini-shell" style="--mini-nav: 2rem"><span>bar</span><span></span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted"><strong>Rail</strong> — <code>md</code>…<code>lg</code>, or collapsed by the visitor</p></div>
	<div class="im-stack im-stack-xs"><div class="mini-shell" style="--mini-nav: 0rem"><span>bar</span><span></span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted"><strong>Drawer</strong> — below <code>md</code></p></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<ul>
	<li><strong>Rail.</strong> Labels, group titles, counts and tree children are hidden with CSS only — they stay in the DOM for screen readers — and each link's <code>title</code> supplies the tooltip. So always give a nav link a <code>title</code> and an icon.</li>
	<li><strong>The visitor's choice</strong> is <code>&lt;html data-nav="rail"&gt;</code>, toggled by any <code>[data-nav-toggle]</code>, stored, and applied before first paint by <code>partials/shell/head-script.hbs</code> — so the page never jumps.</li>
	<li><strong>On a phone.</strong> Below <code>md</code> the side nav leaves the grid and its links become tiles in the <a href="/navigation/navbar/#menu-panel">menu panel</a> — a group of links becomes a tile that opens.</li>
	<li><strong>It scrolls on its own</strong>, under the bar, with a scrollbar that only appears on hover; a footer (<code>im-sidenav-foot</code>) sticks to its bottom.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Structure</h2>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<aside class="im-sidenav" aria-label="Sections">
	<div class="im-navgroup">
		<p class="im-navgroup-title">Writing</p>
		<a class="im-navlink" href="/journal/" title="Journal" aria-current="page">{{> "icons/book-open"}}<span>Journal</span></a>
		…
	</div>
	<p class="im-sidenav-foot">© 2026</p>
</aside>
{{{{/code}}}}
<p>In Ghost, <code>\{{navigation as="side"}}</code> renders the site's navigation as <code>im-navlink</code>s (without icons — Ghost's navigation has none; add them by matching on <code>slug</code> in <code>partials/navigation.hbs</code> if you want them).</p>

